Subject: [PATCH v10 09/14] ALSA: virtio: add staged capture accounting and lifecycle recovery
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:26:24 +0900
Message-ID: <20261030052629.27742-10-mynameisjune111@gmail.com>
X-Mailer: git-send-email 2.54.0
In-Reply-To: <20261030052629.27742-1-mynameisjune111@gmail.com>
References: <20261030052629.27742-1-mynameisjune111@gmail.com>
X-Mailing-List: virtualization@lists.linux.dev
List-Id: <virtualization.lists.linux.dev>
List-Post: <mailto:virtualization@lists.linux.dev>
List-Help: <mailto:virtualization+help@lists.linux.dev>
List-Subscribe: <mailto:virtualization+subscribe@lists.linux.dev>
List-Unsubscribe: <mailto:virtualization+unsubscribe@lists.linux.dev>
List-Owner: <mailto:virtualization+owner@lists.linux.dev>
Precedence: list
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Staged capture needs request-owned DMA storage and separate produced,
observed and consumed positions when shared clients use a boundary stop
threshold. Synchronize that policy with RX completion and acknowledgment.
Keep native device running state, RELEASE obligations and reset epochs
separate from the ALSA runtime state.

Serialize prepare, sync_stop, hw_params and hw_free with a lifecycle
mutex. Bind control messages to their originating epoch at enqueue and
retain request storage until device ownership ends. Keep the short,
packed, empty and pause-restart compatibility options disabled by default.

Exclude prepare from playback and capture ACK with each member's
buffer_mutex. Linked
prepare marks buffer_accessing negative only on its initiating member,
so testing that counter leaves later members exposed. Use a trylock from
the PCM-locked ACK path to preserve the buffer-to-PCM locking order.

Check the PCM state under its stream lock after acquiring lifecycle_lock
in sync_stop. Trigger holds that lock through its control requests; a
replacement active generation must retain its device state. Prepare
cannot replace an inactive generation while lifecycle_lock is held.

Refill staged RX descriptors after a definitely rejected native pause.
If recovery cannot establish a usable queue, latch XRUN and retain the
teardown obligation. Check for a detached virtqueue under its queue lock
before processing an IRQ callback.

Disable period work until open succeeds and disable it synchronously at
close. Cancel pending work after hw_free teardown even on error. This
also prevents error paths from queuing work after runtime release.

Forced interleavings reproduced the NULL-queue crash, false ACK XRUN,
empty RX queue after pause rejection and stale sync_stop interference.
The corrected paths passed recovery and reopen with KASAN and lockdep.
A forced playback ACK during prepare also reproduced stale accounting
and a first-write XRUN; the per-runtime trylock prevents that mutation.
Tests also rejected late work after close and exercised freeze, failed
restore and recovery. The original UAF itself was not reproduced.

The separate PCM notification helper supplies subperiod wakeups. RESET
conversion and notification priority follow in their own patches.

